course: dictionary
lesson: 16083
title: Words for singing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a sound so well that you can almost hear it. Warble is one of them. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «In spring, the blackbird began to warble from the top of the oak tree.» The birds are singing, the sound is sweet, and it is in spring, so warble means to sing sweetly.
explain: Warble can also be used for people. «Grandad warbled an old song in the bath, a bit wobbly and very loud.» Grandad is a person, not a bird, so warble here means to sing in a high, wobbly voice. The word "wobbly" is a clue, and the writer is being gently funny.
explain: Warble can be a noun too. «The warble of the blackbird filled the garden.» Here warble is the sound itself, not the action. Use the words around it to tell which one it is: a verb shows what someone does, and a noun names a thing.
fact: Warble means to sing with a sweet, trembling, changing sound.
fact: Birds warble in the trees, especially in spring.
fact: «Grandad warbled an old song in the bath.» This means he sang in a high, wobbly voice, and it is often said as a joke.
fact: As a noun, a warble is a warbling sound.
fact: Warblers are small songbirds, and they are named after their song.
exercise: «The robin began to warble on the fence.» What does warble mean here? | To fall off the fence | To shout angrily at the cat | To build a nest | *To sing with a sweet, trembling sound
exercise: «Grandad warbled an old song in the bath, a bit wobbly and very loud.» What does warbled mean? | Fell asleep in the water | Dried himself with a towel | Shouted at the plumber | *Sang in a high, wobbly voice
exercise: «The warble of the blackbird filled the garden.» Find and copy the word that means a sweet, trembling sound. | *warble | blackbird | garden | filled
test: «Warblers are small songbirds named after their song.» What are warblers named after? | *Their song | Their colour | Their nests | Their size
test: Maya says a bird that warbles is shouting. What does warble really mean for a bird? | A bird shouting at a cat | *A bird singing with a sweet, trembling, changing sound | A bird flying very fast | A bird sleeping in a tree
exam: «In spring, the birds warbled, and the children laughed at Grandad's wobbly song.» What does warbled mean for the birds? | Fell silent | *Sang with a sweet, trembling, changing sound | Shouted rudely at the children | Flew away in a hurry
